{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>Tempered.</b> As the Targum renders it: מְעֹרָב — mixed, that he should blend their grinding well, this with that. And I say that it is like ״וַיִּרְאוּ הַמַּלָּחִים״ (Jonah 1), ״מַּלָּחַיִךְ וְחֹבְלָיִךְ״ (Ezekiel 27) — so called because they turn the waters with oars when they steer the ship, like a person who beats beaten eggs to mix them with water; and anything a person wants to blend well, he turns it with a finger or with a בָּזֵךְ." "<b>Tempered, pure, sacred.</b> It shall be tempered, and it shall be pure, and it shall be sacred."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "Old French bazec / modern French fouet — a whisk."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:54.000375820Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}